{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an unattended coordinator) launches me repeatedly as an INDEPENDENT adjudicator in lane worktrees of the ai-template repo, a meta-project that ships a gated, requirement-traced process kit under project-trajectory/. Each request is one of:\n   - **A dispute sitting:** rule each finding FIX / SUCCESSOR / DISMISS (`out-of-scope`, `refuted` or `not-worth-cost`) / ESCALATE, within PROCESS.md §6 \"Review threat model\", including its plausibility test. A cheap fix for a contrived scenario is still DISMISS. Write `RULING:` lines.\n   - **An amendment sitting:** rule each amended approved row CLARITY or MEANING. The new protocol adds `[MEANING+BLESS]`, meaning a MEANING row I would bless; plain `[MEANING]` means not blessed and returned via `## Dispositions`. End with `VERDICT: MEANING|CLARITY rows=N`.\n   - **A first-approval sitting:** rule each `Drafted` row APPROVE or RETURN, ending with `OUTCOME: APPROVE|RETURN rows=N`.\n   - **A done-when sitting:** a single-kind verdict ending `DONE-WHEN: CLARITY|BLESSED|SUCCESSOR changes=N digest=<verbatim>`.\n   - **A combined sitting:** one `## <kind>` heading per kind, ending `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=...`.\n   - **An act turn (new protocol):** take only the listed snapshot acts from a committed verdict, each in its own commit ending with the trailer `WI: WI-NNN`.\n\n   Commit each verdict once with the trailer `WI: WI-NNN`. In the old protocol I also took the acts myself; in the new protocol the sitting stops at the committed verdict.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **The spine:** SN → SR → LLR → TC registries (docs/requirements/*.toml, docs/test/test-cases.toml); `docs/archive/last_approved` holds the snapshot anchor, and `acts.toml` is the act ledger.\n   - **The approval dial:** `human_approval_through = \"DevStg-Boundary\"` in docs/process.toml. The SR, LLR and TC rungs are released.\n   - **Snapshot commands:** `python project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py snapshot --reattests IDS` and `--approves \"reg=WI-NNN;reg=WI-NNN\"` (quoted). The snapshot refuses if another approved row in a copied registry has drifted.\n   - **Validators:**\n     - `kitlib.sitting.parse(text, brief, kinds)` and `sitting_refusal(text, where, kinds)`;\n     - `kitlib.verdict.blessed_rows(text)` and `row_rulings(section, kind)`;\n     - `kitlib.sitting.own_section(text, kind, keyword)`;\n     - `kitlib.dispute.parse(text, requested)`;\n     - `adjudicate_act.left_owed(root, verdict, rev='HEAD')`, where None means nothing is owed.\n   - **Judging rules applied:**\n     - one decision per row, one home;\n     - an AC must observe obligations the Requirement states;\n     - SR and SN rows name no files, and LLRs name no implementation carriers;\n     - TC Tier is the whole cited set's (slow-only modules listed in tests/conftest.py SLOW_MODULES make the tier `Full`);\n     - a TC must not claim more than its cited Evidence and verified rows carry.\n   - **Owner rulings** cited across lanes: D-011 (contrived-guards audit), D-008, D-014, D-016, D-019, D-012, D-013.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (verdicts written and act commits; all committed):\n   - **docs/reviews/wi-902/:**\n     - **004-ADJUDICATE-d8779c8.md:** DA FIX. Title match imports unrelated lineage; reproduced with a probe in the scratchpad.\n     - **006-ADJUDICATE-a52f1fb.md:** amendment MEANING rows=7, with LLR-153 and TC-147 not blessed; first-approval RETURN on LLR-335 and TC-360 (two homes for one decision). Act: re-attested SR-148.\n     - **007-ADJUDICATE-48b41d7.md:** amendment MEANING rows=6, all blessed; first-approval APPROVE on LLR-335 and TC-360. Acts taken.\n     - **009-ADJUDICATE-653e96e.md:** DB FIX. A refused landing sweep was replayed as if consumed (`_lande